    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "components. Most people don't really care if you \nhave an Acer or an HP laptop. They care about the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 923040,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "specs and the components. And as cars become more \nappliance-like, there is really nothing separating  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 927920,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "them from the same fate. Which leads us neatly \nonto the China problem. We briefly touched on it,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 934080,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but Chinese EVs and hybrids are here and their \ncost to performance ratio is very hard to compete  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 939280,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with. Now, in America, this hasn't mattered yet \nbecause trade barriers keep us isolated to the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 944880,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "point that we really do live in our own little \ncar bubble. A lot of the most popular cars in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 950080,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "North America simply don't exist outside of North \nAmerica. Seeing an F-150 in Europe, for example,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 956080,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is extremely rare. This is either because our \ncars are too large for roads in other major  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 960800,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "markets of Europe and Asia, too inefficient for \nlocal laws, or because there are just better,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 965280,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cheaper local alternatives. Now, that's typically \nbeen fine for us at least, because the USA is such  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 971280,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a large market that even foreign automakers \nset up operations here to get inside the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 975600,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bubble. But there are a lot of manufacturers, \nparticularly those from Europe and Japan,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 979760,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that depend far more heavily on exporting cars \nbeyond their home country. And for a long time,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 984720,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the single largest and fastest growing market was \nChina itself. European automakers in particular  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 990400,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "enjoyed several years of selling high-end cars to \nstatus-driven consumers in the rapidly developing  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 995600,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chinese economy. And for most of that time, they \nreally didn't have any competition because locally  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1000800,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "produced Chinese cars were almost embarrassingly \ncheap, poorly engineered, lacking in features,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1005440,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and most importantly, they couldn't compete \nwith the status of the European luxury brands.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1010240,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that has clearly changed. Even despite being \nlargely protected from Chinese competition on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1015280,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their home turf, European automakers have run \ninto a serious problem trying to sell their cars  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1020160,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into China because local alternatives \nare now far more competitive. Xiaomi,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1025280,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a company that didn't even have a car division 5 \nyears ago, delivered over 400,000 vehicles in its  "
    } ]
  }, {
